+
+**Task ID:** `bridge-20261030-premise-delivered-residual-r1` · **Agent:** GLM Agent 22 (Job 486813) · **Date:** 2026-10-30T11:0xZ · **Base:** origin/main `1f2c864` · **Refs** #3194 (landed fix, commit `139b73e`) · #3193 · #3157 · #3169 · #3180 · #3182 — no close, verdict plane decides.
+
+**বাংলা সারসংক্ষেপ:** #3194-এর premise-delivered demotion চমৎকার ল্যান্ড হয়েছে, কিন্তু তার Scan B শুধু **মার্জড** PR-এর citation-এ সক্রিয় হয় — আর in-gates WO-কে ইচ্ছাকৃতভাবে বাদ দেয় ("unmerged/in-gates vehicles never demote")। আজ লাইভে দেখা গেছে ঠিক সেই pre-merge জানালাতেই treadmill ডুপ্লিকেট serve মিন্ট করতে থাকে। এই রিসিট ওই residual-এর ম্যাপ + একটি অপশন (বাণিজ্য-বিশ্লেষণসহ) verdict plane-এর জন্য জমা দেয় — কোনো drive-by কোড পরিবর্তন নয়, কারণ ওটা #3194-এর সদ্য-সিদ্ধ পলিসি সিদ্ধান্ত।
+
+## The residual (live witnesses, this session)
+
+Scan B's posture — "only a merged receipt is a definitive landing signal" — leaves the **in-gates window** (WO filed → PR merged) unmapped. Three pick cycles in one hour witnessed exactly that window minting duplicate serves:
+
+| time (UTC) | event | in-flight vehicle at dispatch time |
+|---|---|---|
+| 10:26Z | loop dispatched **#2395** | WO **#3157** filed 10:25:24Z (1 min earlier), in gates |
+| ~10:34Z | loop dispatched **#2792** | WO **#3169** filed 10:29:03Z, in gates |
+| 10:36Z | #2395 re-dispatch minted duplicate noop WO **#3182** | GLM Agent 22's own WO **#3180** (10:33:59Z), in gates |
+
+Scan A (promised-artifact existence) also does not fire here: none of these rows' bodies promise backticked repo paths. So a fresh agent dispatched onto any of these rows during the window can only produce another duplicate receipt — the U4 founding class, surviving inside the merged-only boundary.
+
+## Option for the verdict plane (design offered, decision theirs)
+
+Extend scan B with a **board-local open-WO title scan** (zero network — the WO rows sit on the same board list the picker already holds):
+
+- WO row = title carries `bridge work order` or labels carry `bridge:queued`; state open.
+- Reference shape = remediation-intent regex `\bfor\s+(?:issue\s+)?#?(\d+)\b` — deliberately NOT bare-citation shapes (`receipt #N`, `Refs #N`), which name evidence chains without remediation intent.
+- Ordering token (the #3050-family monotonic argument): WO number > target number proves the WO was filed after the row it serves; self-references structurally excluded.
+- Fail-open: only REMOVES a dispatch, never blocks; malformed rows serve unchanged; pure mode (claim_probe=None) byte-identical.
+
+**Tradeoff, named honestly:** in-gates WOs can be REJECTED by intake (REJECTED verdicts exist), so this widens the false-suppression surface relative to the merged-only posture — a row whose WO dies in gates would need manual re-serve or a TTL on the demotion. That is precisely why this rides as report-only: the posture change belongs to the plane that owns #3194's design.
+
